# v0.25.12 — post-v0.25.11 work

**Baseline**: `v0.25.11` finalised at `fc356f5169` (2026-10-16). Sections below cover commits accrued on `main` after it, per the release-tag policy (`AGENTS.md`: the version's changelog is finalised in the tagged commit; later entries go to the next version's log).
**Date**: 2026-10-16.
**Tag**: `v0.25.12` (pending).

### CHAIN-STALL-1: alert when the chain head stops moving; favicon link; STATUS.md refresh

- `373062b0` — `ChainHeadStalled` (critical, `aitbc_rules.yml`): fires when
  `aitbc_messaging_chain_head_height` — the RPC process's scrape-time
  `max(block.height)` from the chain DB — has not advanced for 15 min, held
  2 min. Closes the gap where every node is up but stuck at one height
  (the 2026-08-24/25 stalls): `ServiceDown` needs a dead target and
  `SyncLagHigh` needs a peer ahead, so neither fires. Quiet until 15 min of
  history exist and on an empty node. promtool cases cover a stall, an
  advancing node, an empty node and the no-history window;
  `monitoring-setup.md` explains one host firing versus all of them. Not
  deployed: copy the rule file per `check-rules-deployed.sh`, then reload.
- `49044185` — `website/favicon.svg` is a relative symlink to `AITBC.svg`
  instead of `/opt/aitbc/website/AITBC.svg`, which dangled in any checkout
  outside `/opt/aitbc` and failed the website link and asset-stamp guards
  there. The committed stamp already matches; no restamp.
- `dbd6ff58` — `STATUS.md`: rows for v0.25.8–v0.25.11 and a dated
  current-topology section (five hosts, four validators, 3-of-4
  attestations with PBFT off, KR-5 rotation, v10–v14 heights, Sepolia-only
  bridge) ahead of the August history it used to present as live.

### docs(release): relocate post-tag entries from the v0.25.9 log to v0.25.11

- `f35a3df1` — the v0.25.9 tag froze its log, but 30 `### ` sections and a
  283-line commit index (2026-10-14/15 work, all inside the v0.25.11
  window) had been appended to it afterwards. They move to
  `v0.25.11_change.log`: sections appended in order, the hash list under a
  new `### Commit index` section so the coverage check still resolves
  every hash. `v0.25.9_change.log` matches its tag again except the
  retained internal-host-token scrub.

### CHAIN-STALL-2 + OPS: missing-gauge alert, deploy-rules.sh, STATUS.md order

- `defc3af3` — `ChainHeadMetricMissing` (warning, `aitbc_rules.yml`):
  `ChainHeadStalled` reads `aitbc_messaging_chain_head_height`, so a
  target answering scrapes but exposing no series leaves the stall rule
  blind. Fires when `up{job="blockchain-node"} == 1` but the gauge is
  absent for 10m; promtool cases cover reporting/blind/dead instances.
- `12afad17` — `scripts/monitoring/deploy-rules.sh`: the write side of
  `check-rules-deployed.sh`. Derives the rule-file list from
  prometheus.yml, promtool-checks the repo copy before and the deployed
  copy after, reloads prometheus only once everything validates;
  `--no-reload` for staged deploys. Fleet deploys become copy → check →
  reload in one step instead of three.
- `d9ff3f18` — STATUS.md: the v0.25.5 row moves back between v0.25.4 and
  v0.25.6; it had drifted to the bottom of the v0.25 block.
